# ── Version ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stamp this version into the bundle instead of the one in Info.plist.
# CI passes the git tag here; a leading "v" is stripped.
# CATNAP_VERSION=2.0.0

# ── Toolchain workarounds ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Extra flags appended to every `swift` command inside build.sh. Only needed
# where SwiftPM's manifest sandbox cannot start (nested sandboxes / some
# containers); normal machines and GitHub runners must leave this empty.
# CATNAP_SWIFT_FLAGS=--disable-sandbox

# ── Code Signing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Developer ID Application certificate identity, e.g.
#   Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)
# `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` lists what is installed.
# Leave empty for an ad-hoc signature (users must clear the quarantine flag).
CATNAP_SIGNING_IDENTITY=

# ── Notarization ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option A: Keychain profile (preferred)
# Store credentials first with:
#   xcrun notarytool store-credentials "PROFILE_NAME" \
#     --apple-id "you@example.com" \
#     --team-id "XXXXXXXXXX" \
#     --password "xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx"
# Then set the profile name here:
CATNAP_NOTARY_PROFILE=

# Option B: Inline credentials (fallback if no keychain profile)
# CATNAP_APPLE_ID=you@example.com
# CATNAP_TEAM_ID=XXXXXXXXXX
# CATNAP_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx

# ── Sparkle update signing ────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT read from this file: the EdDSA private key is a GitHub repository secret
# (`SPARKLE_ED_PRIVATE_KEY`) and is only used by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# Locally it lives at ~/.config/letmecatnap/sparkle_ed25519_private.key.
# The matching public key is committed in Info.plist as SUPublicEDKey.
